            <ArticleTitle>Myositis ossificans complicating severe Guillain-Barré syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>775-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report myositis ossificans occurring in a 13-year-old boy with severe and rapidly progressive Guillain-Barré syndrome. This complication should be considered when severe musculoskeletal pain is experienced by such patients. Disodium etidronate may be of benefit in this condition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
